        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Hawaiian tropical dry forests, leeward Hawaiian island slopes\n- Products: Acacia koa, Acacia koaia, Euphorbia species, wiliwili\n- Concepts: Fabaceae, flowering trees, elevation ranges\n\nFacts:\n- Hawaiian tropical dry forests have dominant tree species that include koa (Acacia koa), koaiʻa (Acacia koaia), and ʻakoko (Euphorbia species).\n- Acacia koa is a species of flowering tree in the pea family Fabaceae.\n- Wiliwili is typically found in Hawaiian tropical dry forests on leeward island slopes up to an elevation of 600 meters.",
